      "text": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>Partially Budget party for solo giratina. Try to run Mega ray with decent uptime, using necrozma for simple catch tanking, and hopefully running all your party+ 1 sponged shadow ball on your rayquaza for a clean win.</p><h4>Est Time to Win</h4><p>280-290s likely, assuming NAE and generic aggression</p><h2>Main Strategy</h2><p>The main strategy involves using a leading main DPS pokemon, (best choice eternatus, alternative equal being mega ray( moveset DT/BS)) as your on field damage dealer. Expect this pokemon to take the brunt of the boss's uptime on the field and mostly use it when the boss is not doing charge attacks on you. When triggering a charge attack, use a substitute dawn wings necrozma (needs around minimum lvl 44, to avoid KO after MGB) to catch the hit, and launch a charge attack in retribution. Relobby when out of catch tanks, and your main dps rayquaza is under 30% HP, since it gets KO'd by shadow ball. Rinse and repeat, and Happy Halloween. If however you have the budget, definitely run the eternatus main DPS!</p><h2>Video Credits</h2><p><br></p>",
